lease click the \",t_note2_2:\"Next\",t_note2_3:\" button.\",t_note3_1:\"To exit, please click the \",t_note3_2:\"Exit\",t_note3_3:\" button.\"},qspassword:{et:\"Quick Setup - Password\",title:\"Change Login Password\",t_tip:\"Username and password can contain between 1 - 15 characters and may not include spaces.\",t_oldname:\"Old User Name\",t_oldpwd:\"Old Password\",t_newname:\"New User Name\",t_newpwd:\"New Password\",t_cfmpwd:\"Confirm Password\"},qsMode:{et2:\"Quick Setup - Operation Mode\",t_mode:\"Choose Operation Mode:\",sysmod1:\"Wireless Router\",router_info:\"Share Internet connection from an Ethernet cable.For example,hotel room,small office...\",sysmod2:\"Access Point\",ap_info:\"Set up Wi-Fi on an existing wired network\",sysmod3:\"Range Extender\",repeater_info:\"Extend the range of an existing Wi-Fi\",sysmod4:\"Client\",client_info:'Act as a \"Wireless Adapter\" to connect your wired devices(e.g.Blu-ray player,smart TV) to existing Wi-Fi',sysmod5:\"Multi-SSID\",mssid_info:\"Create multiple wireless networks to provide different security and VLAN groups.\",sysmod6:\"WISP\",hotspot_info:\"Share Internet connection anywhere public Wi-Fi exists. For example: hotel room, trade show, ...\",sysmod7:\"3G/4G Router\",modem_info:\"Share Internet connection from 3G or 4G modem.\"},qsWlScanClient:{et:\"AP List\",t_info:\"The scanned APs are as follows\",t_aps:\"AP numbers:\",t_signal:\"Signal strength\"},qsWlHotspot:{et:\"Quick Setup - Wireless\",t_cli:\"Client Setting\",t_ap:\"AP Setting\",t_brssid:\"SSID(to be bridged)\",t_brbssid:\"MAC Address(to be bridged)\",t_eg:\"e.g. 00:1D:0F:11:22:33\",t_wepidx:\"WEP Index:\",t_scan:\"Scan\",t_localwlname:\"Local Network SSID\"},qsWlClient:{et:\"Quick Setup - Wireless\",t_brssid:\"SSID(to be bridged):\",t_brbssid:\"MAC Address(to be bridged):\",t_wdsdetect:\"AddrMode:\",t_wepidx:\"WEP Index:\",repeater_wlname:\"Wireless Name of Range Extender\",t_copy:\"Copy from Root AP\",t_scan:\"Scan\",t_custom:\"Customize\"},qsWlAP:{et:\"Quick Setup - Wireless\",et_2g:\"Quick Setup - Wireless 2.4G\",t_more:\"More Advanced Wireless Settings\",},qsWlAP5G:{et:\"Quick Setup - Wireless 5GHz\",t_more:\"More Advanced Wireless Settings\"},qsLan:{et:\"Quick Setup - Network Setting\",t_smart:\"Smart IP(DHCP)\",t_lantype1:\"Note: The IP parameters cannot be configured if you have chosen Smart IP(DHCP)\",t_lantype2:\"(In this situation the device will help you configure the IP parameters automatically as you need).\",t_lantype3:\"We recommend you configure this AP with the same IP subnet and subnet mask, but different IP address from your root AP/Router.\"},qsReview:{et:\"Quick Setup - Review Setting\",t_congraduation:\"Congratulations! The settings is finish, please click finish button to make it work.For detailed settings, please click other menus if necessary.\",t_change:\"Changing work mode should be reboot!\",t_confirm:\"Confirm the configuration you have set. If anything wrong,please go Back to reset.\",t_recommend:\"It's recommented to take a note of these settings that you'll need later for reference.\",t_wl:\"Wireless Settings\",t_operamode:\"Operation Mode:\",t_ssid:\"Wireless Network Name(SSID):\",t_channel:\"Wireless Channel:\",t_secmode:\"Wireless Security Mode:\",t_operamode_5g:\"Operation Mode:\",t_ssid_5g:\"Wireless Network Name(SSID):\",t_channel_5g:\"Wireless Channel:\",t_secmode_5g:\"Wireless Security Mode:\",t_lan:\"LAN Settings\",t_defaultAccess:\"Default Access:\",t_lantype:\"LAN Type:\",t_connen:\"Connect to Host Network:\",t_connen_5g:\"Connect to Host Network:\",t_brssid:\"SSID(to be bridged):\",t_brssid_5g:\"SSID(to be bridged):\"},qsMultiSSID:{et:\"Multi-SSID Wireless Setting\",t_envlan:\"Enable VLAN:\",t_on:\"ON\",t_off:\"OFF\",t_channel:\"Channel:\",t_ssid1:\"SSID 1:\",t_vlan1:\"VLAN ID:\",t_ssid2:\"SSID 2:\",t_vlan2:\"VLAN ID:\",t_ssid3:\"SSID 3:\",t_vlan3:\"VLAN ID:\",t_ssid4:\"SSID 4:\",t_vlan4:\"VLAN ID:\"},qsDsl:{et:\"Quick Setup - DSL\",t_info1:\"Please enter the VPI/VCI provided by your ISP(Internet Service Provider).\",t_info2:\"Or you can enable the PVC Auto-detection.\",t_auto:\"Enable PVC Auto-detection\"},qsType:{et1:\"Quick Setup - ADSL Connection Type\",et2:\"Quick Setup - WAN Connection Type\",t_info:\"Please select the connection type provided by your ISP.\",t_auto_info:\"Let the router automatically detect the internet connection type provided by your ISP.\",t_ppp_info1:\"(Requires a username and password for PPP over Ethernet)\",t_ppp_info2:\"You have DSL connection and is connected via PPPoE (Broadband Connection) on your computer or existing router.\",t_pppoa_info:\"(Requires a username and password for PPP over ATM)\",t_dhcp_info1:\"(Obtain Dynamic IP from ISP, also called IPoE Dynamic IP)\",t_dhcp_info2:\"For Cable/DSL/Broadband connection which makes your computer immediately online without any setting or signing-in.\",t_staip_info1:\"(Manually set the static IP address provided by your ISP, also called IPoE Static IP)\",t_staip_info2:\"Your ISP provides you specified IP parameters.\",t_ipoa_info:\"(Manually set the static IP address provided by your ISP, also called IP Over ATM)\",t_br_info:\"(Dial up from a single computer or router)\",eoa_info:\"Note: IPoA &amp; PPPoA doesn't support single-PVC-multi-connection. They are disabled for connections already existing in this PVC.\",t_tip:\"The Quick Setup is preparing to set up your internet connection, please choose one type below according to your ISP. The detailed description will be displayed after you choose the corresponding type.\",t_autoDetect:\"Auto-Detect\",t_pppoe_ru:\"PPPoE/Russia PPPoE\",t_l2tp_ru:\"L2TP/Russia L2TP \",t_pptp_ru:\"PPTP/Russia PPTP \",t_note:\"Note: For users in some areas(such as Russia, Ukraine etc.), please contact your ISP to choose connection type manually.\",t_l2tp_info1:\"In this type, you should fill in the username, password and IP address/Domain name of VPN Server provided by your ISP. Auto-Detect can't detect this connection type.\",t_pptp_info1:\"In this type, you should fill in the username, password and IP address/Domain name of VPN Server provided by your ISP. Auto-Detect can't detect this connection type.\",t_more:\"More Advanced Settings\",t_iptvmode:\"IPTV Mode:\"},qsDetectErr:{t_reasons:\"The router is failed to detect your internet connection type, the following are the most likely reasons:\",t_reason1:\"1. The router was not power cycled.\",t_reason1Detail:\"To solve this problem, please power cycle your router(turn if off and on) and wait 2 minutes to finish its initialization. If your router has a backup battery, please remove and reinsert its battery.\",t_reason2:\"2. The hardware connection is wrong.\",t_reason2Detail:\"To solve this problem, please double-check the internet port(blue port) is fully inserted with the Ethernet cable from your router or other network device.\",t_reason3:\"3. Your ISP(Internet Service provider) assigned a fixed(static) IP to you.\",t_reason3Detail:\"The router can not automatically detect such rare special network type, you need to enter the parameters manully.\",t_options:\"Select one of the options below and click Next to preceed:\",t_dhcp_info1:\"Now I will reboot my router, wait for 2 minutes and proceed; Usually this operation will resolve most of the issues.\",t_macclone_info1:\"I've rebooted the router before, now I will try to clone the MAC address from my original computer.\",t_staip_info1:\"Yes, my ISP assigns me a fixed IP address.\"},qsPPP:{et:\"Quick Setup - PPPoE\",t_info:\"Please enter the Username and Password. If the Username/Password are unknown, please contact your ISP.\",t_secondConn:\"Secondary Connection\",t_forDual:\"&nbsp;(For Dual Access)\"},qsL2tp:{et:\"Quick Setup - L2TP\",t_info:\"Please enter the Username and Password. If you forget them, please consult your ISP.\"},qsPptp:{et:\"Quick Setup - PPTP\",t_info:\"Please enter the Username and Password. If you forget them, please consult your ISP.\"},qsStaIP:{et:\"Quick Setup - Static IP\",t_info:\"Please enter the basic parameter settings provided by your ISP. If basic parameters are unknown, please contact ISP.\"},qsPPPoA:{et:\"Quick Setup - PPPoA\",t_info:\"Please enter ADSL Username and Password. If the Username/Password are unknown, please contact ISP.\"},qsIPoA:{et:\"Quick Setup - IPoA\",t_info:\"Please enter the basic parameter settings provided by your ISP. If basic parameters are unknown, please contact ISP.\"},qs3g:{et:\"Quick Setup - 3G/4G\",t_info:\"3G/4G can be set as a backup method for Internet Access. If you wish not to configure 3G/4G settings now, click Next and continue. Otherwise, enable the 3G/4G Backup to apply configurations.\",t_no_isp_start:\"If your location or ISP is not listed, or the default Dial Number/ APN may need to be updated, please enable to set configurations manually.\",t_no_isp_end:\", and fill in the right ones.\"},qsAuto:{et:\"Quick Setup - Auto\",t_detect:\"Detecting the connection type your ISP provides, please wait...\"},qsMacClone:{et:\"Quick Setup - MAC Clone\",t_mac_tip:'MAC(Media Access Control) address is a unique identifier that identifies your computer or device in the network. Some of the ISPs may register the MAC address of your computer which firstly connects to their services, and would not allow the Internet connection for any new computer or router. TP-Link router can help you to \"clone\" or replicate the registered MAC address of your first computer.',t_suggestion:\"In most of the cases, there is no need to clone the MAC address. But if you can't get the Internet connection after Quick Setup, please run it again and clone the MAC address for a try. \",t_noClone:\"No, I do NOT need to clone MAC address.\",t_yesClone:\"YES, I need to clone MAC address.\",t_makeSureNote:\"Note: please make sure your current computer is the one initially connected to your router or ISP's device.\"},qsBandSelect:{et:\"Quick Setup - Wireless Dual Band Selection\",t_note:\"Please select or clear the check box to enable or disable a given radio band.\"},qsWl:{et:\"Quick Setup - Wireless\",et_2g:\"Quick Setup - Wireless 2.4GHz\",t_more:\"More Advanced Wireless Settings\"},qsWl5G:{et:\"Quick Setup - Wireless 5GHz\",t_more:\"More Advanced Wireless Settings\"},qsSave:{et:\"Quick Setup - Confirm\",t_info:\"The Quick Setup is complete. Please confirm all parameters below. Click BACK to modify any settings or click SAVE to save and apply your configurations.\",t_summary:\"Parameters Summary:\",t_note:\"Note: Some connections will be deleted:\"},qsEnd:{et:\"Quick Setup - Complete\",t_stat:\"Setup Status:\",t_mode:\"Operation Mode Configuring:\",t_pvc:\"PVC Detecting:\",t_release:\"WAN Connection Releasing:\",t_wan:\"WAN Connection Configuring:\",t_gw:\"Gateway and DNS Configuring:\",t_wl:\"Wi-Fi Configuring:\",t_wl2g:\"Wireless 2.4GHz Configuring:\",t_wl5g:\"Wireless 5GHz Configuring:\",t_iptv:\"IPTV Configuring:\",t_fail:\"PVC Auto-detection failed. Please enter your ISPs PVC parameters and click NEXT. If the PVC parameters are unknown, please contact your ISP for PVC parameter information.\",con_end1:\"Quick Setup is complete. Please click FINISH to exit.\",con_end2:\"Quick Setup is complete! Configurations will no take effect until the device reboots. Please click REBOOT to restart the Router.\",con_end3:'Note: If the Router still can not connect to the Internet, please click \"Network > WAN\" menu on the left to confirm the WAN connection type and mode on the WAN page.',t_retry:\"Some configurations during the Quick Setup may have been lost. Please try again.\",t_def:\"If errors appear again or there is still no Internet connection, please restore Router to its factory defaults and try the Quick Setup again.\"},qsVoiceAcc:{t_et:\"Quick Setup - Voice\",t_info1:'The \"WAN type\" is set to \"Bridged\", Voice is not supported.',t_info2:'Basic Voice parameters can be configured on this page. To skip VoIP configurations, leave \"Profile Name\" blank and click \"Next\".',t_con_haveUVM:'Note: Please set the USB VoiceMail within \"Voice>USB VoiceMail\" or use the EasySetupAssisstant CD.',t_setup:\"Advanced Setup\"},sysMode:{et1:\"Operation Mode\",et2:\"Quick Setup - Operation Mode\",t_mode:\"Select an Operation Mode:\",sysmod1:\"ADSL Modem Router Mode\",sysmod2:\"Wireless Router\",sysmod3:\"Router Mode\",sysmod4:\"Access Point\",sysmod5:\"Client\",sysmod6:\"Range Extender\",sysmod7:\"WISP\",sysmod8:\"Multi-SSID\",sysmod9:\"3G/4G Router\"},wan:{et:\"ADSL WAN Interface\",t_info:\"This page shows the information of the entire ADSL WAN interface.\",t_name:\"Name\",t_type:\"Type\"},div:{et:\"WAN Settings\",t_autoPvc:\"Enable PVC Auto-detection\",t_note1:\"Notice: The current PVC has several connections, the following parameters will prohibit any modifications!\",t_note2:\"Notice: Do not change the parameters below unless necessary!\",t_speDial:\"Special Dial:\"},ethWan:{et:\"WAN Settings\",t_en:\"Enable WAN connection\",t_addrType:\"Addressing Type:\",auto_auth:\"AUTO_AUTH\",t_bpa_authServer:\"Auth Server:\",t_bpa_authDomain:\"Auth Domain:\",authFail:\"Authentication failed, incorrect username or password.\"},usb3g:{et:\"3G/4G Settings\",t_info_start:\"3G/4G Settings are unavailable because the operation mode is not set to 3G/4G Router Mode or 3G/4G backup is not enabled. Please\",t_info_en:\"Enable 3G/4G backup\",t_info_chg:\"or change settings on\",t_info_end:\"to modify any 3G/4G configuration settings.\",t_backup_delay_time:\"Backup Delay\",t_revert_delay_time:\"Revert Delay\",t_3g_modem:\"USB 3G/4G modem\",t_pin_status:\"PIN Status\",card_name_unplugged:\"Unplugged\",card_name_ing:\"Identifying...\",card_name_ok:\"Successfully Identified\",pin_status_fail:\"Failed to connect script\",pin_status_ready:\"Ready\",pin_status_pin:\"PIN Locked\",pin_status_puk:\"PUK Locked\",pin_status_errror:\"Error Unknown\",t_pin_code:\"PIN Code\",pinUnlockBtn:\"Unlock\",t_notice_t:\"Notice\",t_notice:\"You must set the Dial Number and APN manually, please click Advance to modify these configurations.\",t_sysmode_start:\"The current\",t_sysmod_is:\"is\",sysmod_dsl:\"ADSL Modem Router Mode\",sysmod_eth:\"Wireless Router Mode\",t_sysmod_end:\". The Connection Mode and Max Idle Time could not be set manually.\",t_pin_chg_en:\"Enable PIN code change\",t_old_pin:\"Old PIN Code\",t_new_pin1:\"New PIN Code\",t_new_pin2:\"Confirm New PIN Code\",t_mtu:\"MTU size (in bytes)\",t_mtu1480:\"(The default is 1480, do not change unless necessary)\",t_follow_ip:\"Use the following IP address\",t_static_ip:\"Static IP Address\",t_follow_dns:\"Use the following DNS Servers\",t_pri_dns:\"Primary DNS\",t_sec_dns:\"Secondary DNS\",modem_set_Btn:\"Modem Settings\"},usb3gModemList:{et:\"3G/4G USB Modem Settings\",t_id:\"ID\",t_vendor:\"Vendor\",t_model:\"Model\"},usb3gUpload:{et:\"Upload 3G/4G USB Modem Configuration File\",t_file:\"File\",t_info:\"Please Note: If you restore the device's factory default setting, the bin file will be lost.In the event that you do lose the bin file, you will need to re-upload it, or download our latest firmware from\",t_info2:\". The updated firmware will be installed into your 3G/4G Device and restore all of its functions.\",upload:\"Upload\",back:\"Back\"},hw_nat:{et:\"NAT Control Setting\",t_hwnat:\"Current Hardware NAT Status:\",t_softnat:\"Current NAT Status:\",t_note:\"1. Make sure the NAT is enable if you want the Hardware NAT configuration take effect.\",t_tcEn:\"2. If Bandwidth Control is enabled, Hardware NAT will NOT take effect, because these two modules cannot work at the same time.\"},group:{et:\"Interface Grouping\",t_info:\"This page displays all current groups.\",t_wancon:\"WAN Interface\",t_lancon:\"LAN Interface\",t_note1:\"Note: You cannot disable VLAN functionality with an IPTV or Ethernet WAN Connection enabled.\",t_note2:\"Note: You cannot disable VLAN functionality with an Ethernet WAN Connection enabled.\",t_note3:\"Note: You can not move default gateway to another group.\",t_note4:\"Enable the Virtual LAN Ports feature\"},groupAdd:{et:\"Add New Group\",t_name:\"Group Name:\",t_lan:\"Available LAN\",t_added:\"Added Interface\",t_wan:\"Available WAN\",t_note1:\"Note: You can not move default gateway \",t_note2:\" to another group.\"},lan:{et:\"LAN Settings\",t_info:\"This page displays the information of the LAN interface.\",t_pool:\"DHCP Pool\"},lanAP:{et:\"LAN Settings\",t_info:\"This page displays the information of the LAN interface.\",t_pool:\"DHCP Pool\"},lanEdit:{et:\"LAN Settings\",t_info:\"The parameters of the LAN can be configured on this page.\",t_note:\"Note: If the LAN IP Address or the subnet mask has been changed, please ensure the DHCP Address Pool and any static IPs on the network are within the same subnet as the new LAN IP.\",t_ensnoop:\"Enable IGMP Snooping\",t_ensecip:\"Enable Second IP\",t_dhcp:\"DHCP Server:\",t_relay:\"DHCP Relay\",t_poolstart:\"Start IP Address:\",t_poolend:\"End IP Address:\",t_leasetime:\"Leased Time:\",t_leaseval:\"(1~2880 minutes, the default value is 120)\",t_defdomain:\"Default Domain:\",t_remote:\"Remote Server Address:\",t_relay_warn:\"Note: You must disable the NAT of the WAN connection or the DHCP Relay configurations may not take effect!\",t_smart:\"Smart IP(DHCP)\",t_lantype1:\"Note: The IP parameters cannot be configured if you have chosen Smart IP(DHCP)\",t_lantype2:\"(In this situation the device will help you configure the IP parameters automatically as you need).\",t_lantype3:\"We recommend you configure this AP with the same IP subnet and subnet mask, but different IP address from your root AP/Router.\"},lanEditAP:{et:\"LAN Settings\",t_info:\"The parameters of the LAN can be configured on this page.\",t_note:\"Note: If the LAN IP Address or the subnet mask has been changed, please ensure the DHCP Address Pool and any static IPs on the network are within the same subnet as the new LAN IP.\",t_ensnoop:\"Enable IGMP Snooping\",t_ensecip:\"Enable Second IP\",t_dhcp:\"DHCP Server:\",t_relay:\"DHCP Relay\",t_poolstart:\"Start IP Address:\",t_poolend:\"End IP Address:\",t_leasetime:\"Leased Time:\",t_leaseval:\"(1~2880 minutes, the default value is 120)\",t_defdomain:\"Default Domain:\",t_remote:\"Remote Server Address:\",t_relay_warn:\"Note: You must disable the NAT of the WAN connection or the DHCP Relay configurations may not take effect!\",t_smart:\"Smart IP(DHCP)\",t_lantype1:\"Note: The IP parameters cannot be configured if you have chosen Smart IP(DHCP)\",t_lantype2:\"(In this situation the device will help you configure the IP parameters automatically as you need).\",t_lantype3:\"We recommend you configure this AP with the same IP subnet and subnet mask, but different IP address from your root AP/Router.\"},status6:{et:\"IPv6 Status\",t_connType:\"Connection Type\",t_connStatus:\"Connection Status\",t_ip6Addr:\"IPv6 Address\",t_ip6Gw:\"IPv6 Default Gateway\",t_ip6Dns:\"Primary IPv6 DNS\",t_ip6SecDns:\"Secondary IPv6 DNS\",t_lan6cfgtype:\"IPv6 Address Type\",t_assint:\"Associate Interface\",t_interface:\"Interface Name:\"},ethWan6:{t_6to4:\"Tunnel 6to4\",t_ppp_same_sess:\"PPPoE same session with IPv4 connection\",t_dyn_hide_addr_config:\"Only prefix delegation for LAN from the ISP\",t_ppp_hide_addr_config:\"Only prefix delegation for LAN from the ISP\",t_passthrough:\"Pass-Through (Bridge)\"},lan6:{et:\"IPv6 LAN Settings\",t_info:\"The parameters of IPv6 LAN can be configured on this page when IPv6 enabled.\",t_note:\"Note: Only the default group will support IPv6 at this moment.\",t_addrtype:\"Address Auto-Configuration Type\",t_pfxtype:\"Site Prefix Configuration Type\",t_radvd:\"RADVD\",t_rdnss:\"Enable RDNSS\",t_ula:\"Enable ULA Prefix\",t_ulapfx:\"ULA Prefix\",t_ulaplen:\"ULA Prefix Length\",t_dhcp6s:\"DHCPv6 Server\",t_startaddr:\"Start IPv6 Address\",t_endaddr:\"End IPv6 Address\",t_lstime:\"Leased Time\",t_lssec:\"seconds (The default value is 86400)\",t_delegated:\"Delegated\",t_static:\"Static\",t_wan:\"Prefix Delegated WAN Connecti