e extended network settings\",t_scanner:\"Scan\"},wlConnect5G:{opt:\"Connect to Host Network\",t_host_net:\"Network\",t_brssid:\"SSID(to be bridged):\",t_brbssid:\"MAC Address(to be bridged):\",t_wep_notice:\"We do not recommend using the WEP encryption if this device operates in 802.11n mode due to the fact that WEP is not supported by 802.11n specification.\",t_tkip_notice:\"We do not recommend using the TKIP encryption if this device operates in 802.11n mode due to the fact that TKIP is not supported by 802.11n specification.\",t_weptype:\"WEP Key Format: \",t_hex:\"Hexadecimal\",t_wepidx:\"WEP Index:\",t_cpcfg_info:\"The configuration modified here will be automatically synchronized to the extended network settings\",t_scanner:\"Scan\"},wlExtender:{opt:\"Extended Network Settings\",t_ext_net:\"Extended Network\",t_ext_ssid:\"Extended 2.4GHz SSID\",t_ext_security:\"Extended 2.4GHz Security:\",t_wep_notice:\"We do not recommend using the WEP encryption if this device operates in 802.11n mode due to the fact that WEP is not supported by 802.11n specification.\",t_ext_password:\"Extended 2.4GHz Password:\",t_wepidx:\"WEP Index:\"},wlExtender5G:{opt:\"Extended Network Settings\",t_ext_net:\"Extended Network\",t_ext_ssid:\"Extended 5GHz SSID\",t_ext_security:\"Extended 5GHz Security:\",t_wep_notice:\"We do not recommend using the WEP encryption if this device operates in 802.11n mode due to the fact that WEP is not supported by 802.11n specification.\",t_ext_password:\"Extended 5GHz Password:\",t_wepidx:\"WEP Index:\"},clientMode:{et:\"Connect to Host Network\",t_brssid:\"SSID(to be bridged):\",t_brbssid:\"MAC Address(to be bridged):\",t_wep_notice:\"We do not recommend using the WEP encryption if this device operates in 802.11n mode due to the fact that WEP is not supported by 802.11n specification.\",t_tkip_notice:\"We do not recommend using the TKIP encryption if this device operates in 802.11n mode due to the fact that TKIP is not supported by 802.11n specification.\",t_wepidx:\"WEP Index:\",t_scan:\"Scan\"},clientMode5G:{et:\"Connect to Host Network\",t_brssid:\"SSID(to be bridged):\",t_brbssid:\"MAC Address(to be bridged):\",t_wep_notice:\"We do not recommend using the WEP encryption if this device operates in 802.11n mode due to the fact that WEP is not supported by 802.11n specification.\",t_tkip_notice:\"We do not recommend using the TKIP encryption if this device operates in 802.11n mode due to the fact that TKIP is not supported by 802.11n specification.\",t_wepidx:\"WEP Index:\",t_scan:\"Scan\"},usbManage:{et:\"USB Mass Storage\",t_info:\"This page provides the basic information about the USB mass storage device, to configure Storage Sharing/FTP/Media Server, please click the corresponding menu on the left.\",t_usb_con:\"USB Mass storage List:\",t_usb_discon:\"USB Mass storage Disconnected!\",t_step1:\"Click Refresh to detect the USB device. The Router will automatically activate the first two connected USB storage devices or up to eight volumes in total.\",t_step2:'If you would like to use other volumes within your storage device(s), please \"Deactivate\" the unused volumes and \"Activate\" the other desired volumes.',t_step3:'Please click \"Disconnect\" before unplugging your USB device to avoid data loss or damage to the device.',t_dev:\"Supported USB Mass Storage:\",t_devlist:\"hard disk, flash disk or memory card reader\",t_fs:\"Supported File System Type:\",t_fslist:\"FAT32 and NTFS\",t_vol:\"Supported Volumes:\",t_volcnt:\"Only two USB storage devices with up to eight volumes can be activated simultaneously.  Up to four USB storage devices with eighteen volumes will be recognized.\"},usbUserAccount:{et:\"User Accounts\",t_info:\"This page allows you to configure user accounts for Storage Sharing/FTP Server. Please click Set to ensure your configurations take effect.\",t_note:'\"Super User\" has full-access permission to all active volumes and shared folders.',t_chidx:\"Choose Index:\",t_newusr:\"New Username:\",t_newpwd:\"New Password:\",t_apply:\"(Will not take effect until you Apply these modifications.)\"},usbSmbSrv:{et:\"Storage Sharing Settings\",t_info:\"Storage Sharing enables you to share files saved on a USB storage device with other computers on the local network.\",t_stat:\"Server Status\",t_anony:\"Anonymous access to all volumes.\",t_fldtbl:\"Folder Table:\",t_apply:\"(Any modifications to this table will not take effect until you Apply these changes.\",t_shname:\"Share Name\",t_dir:\"Directory\",t_access:\"User Access\",t_facc:\"Full-Access\",t_ronly:\"Read-Only\",t_nacc:\"No-Access\",t_note1:'\"Super User\" has full-access permission (Read & Write) to all shared folders.',t_newfld:\"Add New Folder\",t_note2:\"Storage Sharing function is based upon the NetBIOS/SMB protocol supported by Windows OS and some additional operating systems.\",t_note3:\"Anonymous: All active volume(s) will be shared with no authentication required.\",t_note4:\"You will be able access the shared folders by the following methods:\",t_forwin:\"For Windows OS:\",t_forwin2:'Open the \"Run\" window within the Start menu and enter \\\\\\\\(IP Address) or \\\\\\\\(IP Address)\\\\(Share Name)',t_formac:\"For Mac OS:\",t_formac2:'Open the \"Connect to Server\" window within the Go menu and enter smb://(IP Address) or smb://(IP Address)/(Share Name).'},usbFolderBrowse:{et:\"Folder Browse\",t_info1:\"This page allows to set shared folders along with authorization access for Storage Sharing services. These configurations will not take effect when Anonymous access has been enabled.\",t_info2:\"This page allows you to set shared folders along with authorization access for FTP services.\",t_info3:\"This page allows you to set a scan folder for DLNA media services.\",t_shname:\"Share Name:\",t_dir:\"Directory\",t_browse:\"Browse\",t_hide:\"Hide\",t_tbl:\"User Access Control Table:\",t_vol:\"Select Volume:\",t_selvol:\"--please choose volume--\",t_author:\"Authorization Access\",t_note:'\"Super User\". It has full-access permission (Read & Write) to all active volume(s) and share folder(s).'},ftpSrv:{et:\"FTP Server Settings\",t_info:\"A File Transfer Protocol(FTP) server allows you to share files within the USB storage device across the local or public network. The shared folders must be set including user authorization for each folder(s).\",t_stat:\"Server Status:\",t_acc:\"Internet Access:\",t_iaddr:\"Internet Address:\",alg_notice:\"(The FTP ALG must be enabled before these configurations will take effect.)\",t_port:\"Service Port:\",t_defport:\"(The default is 21. Do not change unless necessary.)\",t_ftbl:\"Folder Table:\",t_apply:\"(Any modifications to this table will not take effect until you Apply these changes.)\",t_shname:\"Share name\",t_dir:\"Directory\",t_usridx:\"User Index\",t_note1:'\"Super User\". It has full-access permission (Read & Write) to all active volume(s) and share folder(s).',t_newfld:\"Add New Folder\",t_note2:\"You can access the shared folders by entering the following domain within Windows Explorer or other FTP software:\",t_note3:\"The FTP server will be restarted causing all current FTP connections to be terminated once you click Apply.\"},dlnaManage:{et:\"Media Server Settings\",t_enable:\"Server Enable\",t_name:\"Server Name:\",t_scan:\"Content Scan:\",t_manual:\"Manual Scan:\",manualScan:\"Scan Now\",t_auto:\"Auto Scan:\",t_every:\"Every\",t_hour:\"hour(s)\",t_tip:\"You have shared the following contents:\",t_id:\"ID\",t_shname:\"Share Name\",t_fldname:\"Folder Name\",addContent:\"Add New Folder\"},printSrv:{et:\"Print Server Settings\",t_stat:\"Server Status:\",online:\"Online\",offline:\"Offline\",print_en:\"Start\",print_dis:\"Stop\"},basicSec:{et:\"Basic Security\",t_stat:\"Firewall\",t_pptp:\"PPTP Pass-through\",t_l2tp:\"L2TP Pass-through\",t_ipsec:\"IPSec Pass-through\"},defGateway:{et:\"Default Gateway Settings\",t_info1:\"Note1:Select a preferred WAN interface as the system default gateway.\",t_info2:\"Note 2: This WAN interface is selected for another group and cannot be selected as the system default gateway.\",t_selwan:\"Select WAN Interface:\"},route:{et:\"Static Route\",t_info:\"This page displays the static route table(s). Click Add New to enter a static route or click Edit to modify an existing entry.\",t_dstip:\"Destination IP Address\"},routeEdit:{et:\"Static Route\",t_info:\"Static Route parameters can be configured on this page.\",t_dstip:\"Destination IP Address:\"},rip:{et:\"RIP Settings\",t_info:\"To activate RIP for the WAN interface, select the desired version and operation of RIP as well as check 'Enable'. To disable RIP on the WAN inteface, uncheck the 'Enable' and click 'Save' to allow configurations to take effect.\",t_note:\"Note: RIP cannot be configured on the WAN interface with NAT enabled.\",t_ver:\"Version\"},defGateway6:{et:\"IPv6 Default Gateway Settings\",t_info:\"Select a preferred WAN interface as the system IPv6 default gateway.\",t_selwan:\"Select WAN Interface\"},route6:{et:\"IPv6 Static Route\",t_info:\"This page displays the IPv6 static route table(s). Click Add New to enter a static route or click Edit to modify an existing entry.\",t_dstip6:\"Destination IPv6 Address/Prefix Length\"},route6Edit:{et:\"IPv6 Static Route\",t_info:\"IPv6 Static Route parameters can be configure on this page.\",t_note:\"Note: This device only supports IPv6 Addresses containing prefix lengths of 8/16/24/32/40/48/56/64.\",t_dstip6:\"Destination IPv6 Address\",t_plen:\"Prefix Length\"},virtualServer:{et:\"Virtual Server\",t_info:\"A virtual server defines the mapping from the WAN service port to the LAN server. All requests from the Internet to the designated service port will be redirected to the device specified by the server IP Address.\",t_port:\"Service Port\",t_interPort:\"Internal Port\"},vtlServEdit:{et:\"Virtual Server\",t_info:\"A virtual server defines the mapping from the WAN service port to the LAN server. All requests from the Internet to the designated service port will be redirected to the device specified by the server IP Address.\",t_note1:\"Note: Virtual Server configurations are only supported when there is an available interface.\",t_note2:\"Service ports assigned to Remote Management or CWMP cannot be utilized.\",t_note3:\"The service port set for Remote Management cannot be utilized.\",t_port:\"Service Port:\",t_cport:\"Common Service Port:\",t_sel:\"---Please Select---\",t_interPort:\"Internal Port:\",t_note4:\"(XX or keep empty. If it's empty, Internal port equals to Service port)\"},portTrigger:{et:\"Port Trigger\",t_info:\"Various applications require multiple connections, for example online games, video conferencing, VoIP, etc.   Due to the internal firewall, these applications will not run effectively with a pure NAT router.In these cases, Port Triggering may provide a solution in improving the performance of these particular applications.\",t_tport:\"Trigger Port\",t_proto:\"Trigger Protocol\",t_oport:\"Open Port\",t_oproto:\"Open Protocol\"},portTrigEdit:{et:\"Port Trigger\",t_info:\"Various applications require multiple connections, for example online games, video conferencing, VoIP, etc.   Due to the internal firewall, these applications will not run effectively with a pure NAT router.In these cases, Port Triggering may provide a solution in improving the performance of these particular applications.\",t_note:\"Note: Port Triggering is only supported when there is an available interface.\",t_tport:\"Trigger Port:\",t_tproto:\"Trigger Protocol:\",t_oport:\"Open Port:\",t_oproto:\"Open Protocol:\",t_cport:\"Common Service Port:\",t_sel:\"---Please Select---\"},dmz:{t_info:\"The DMZ host feature opens all service ports to one local host for bidirectional communication.\",t_status:\"DMZ Status:\",t_hostip:\"DMZ Host IP Address:\"},upnp:{t_info:\"This page displays UPnP status and settings.\",t_status:\"Current UPnP Status:\",t_list:\"Current UPnP Settings List\",t_desc:\"App Description\",t_export:\"External Port\",t_inport:\"Internal Port\"},parentCtrl:{et:\"Parental Controls\",t_info:\"Parental Controls can be used to administer all Internet activity including limiting usage and/or access to specific websites to all clients on the network for a specified period of time.\",t_en:\"Enable Parental Controls\",t_pmac:\"MAC Address Of Parental PC:\",t_curmac:\"MAC Address of Current PC:\",t_copy1:\"Copy to Above\",t_lanmac:\"MAC Address in current LAN:\",t_copy2:\"Copy to\",t_sel:\"--Please Select--\",t_mac1:s_str.macaddr+\"-1\",t_mac2:s_str.macaddr+\"-2\",t_mac3:s_str.macaddr+\"-3\",t_mac4:s_str.macaddr+\"-4\",t_setto:\"Apply To:\",t_start:\"Start Time\",t_end:\"End Time\",t_day:\"Each Day\",t_week:\"Each Week\",t_clear:\"Clear Schedule\",t_url:\"Add URL:\",t_detail:\"Details\",t_apply:\"(Will not take effect until you save these changes)\"},fwRules:{et:\"Access Control Rule Management\",t_info:\"This device can restrict Internet activity for specified LAN hosts. You can set and combine access control rules to effectively manage your network.\",t_en:\"Enable Internet access control\",t_defrule:\"Default Filtering Rules\",t_allow:\"Allow\",t_rule1:\"the packets not specified by any filtering rules to passthrough this device.\",t_deny:\"Deny\",t_rule2:\"the packets not specified by any filtering rules to passthrough this device.\",t_note:\"Note: The device will match the incoming packet with the enabled filtering rules one by one down the list and apply to the first matching rule. If the packet is not specified by any filtering rules within the list, then the Default Filtering Rule will take effect\",t_host:\"LAN Host\",t_target:\"Target\",t_sche:\"Schedule\",t_rule:\"Rule\",edit:\"Edit\"},fwRulesEdit:{et:\"Add Internet Access Control Entry\",t_info:\"An Internet access control rule can be configured on this page.\",t_lan:\"LAN Host:\",t_addlan:\"Add LAN Host\",t_wan:\"Target:\",t_addwan:\"Add Target\",t_sche:\"Schedule:\",t_addsche:\"Add Schedule\",t_action:\"Rule:\",t_direction:\"Direction:\",t_in:\"IN\",t_out:\"OUT\",t_protocol:\"Protocol:\"},fwLan:{et:\"Host Settings\",t_addr:\"Address Info\"},fwLanEdit:{et:\"Add or Edit A Host Entry\"},fwWan:{et:\"Target Settings\",t_detail:\"Details\"},fwWanEdit:{et:\"Add or Edit A Target Entry\",urlMode:\"URL Address\",t_addurl:\"Add URL Address:\",t_detail:\"Detail\",t_apply:\"(Will not take effect until you save these changes)\"},fwSche:{et:\"Schedule Settings\"},fwScheEdit:{et:\"Add or Edit A Schedule Entry\",t_info:\"Schedule can be set on this page.\",t_setto:\"Apply To:\",t_start:\"Start Time\",t_end:\"End Time\",t_day:\"Each Day\",t_week:\"Each Week\",t_clear:\"Clear Schedule\"},ddos:{et:\"Advanced Security\",t_info:\"DDoS Parameters can be set on this page.\",t_dos:\"DoS Protection:\",t_note:\"Note: DoS Protection will not take effect when Traffic Statistics is enabled.\",t_icmp:\"Enable ICMP-Flood Attack Filtering\",t_icmpth:\"ICMP-Flood Packets Threshold\",t_udp:\"Enable UDP-Flood Attack Filtering\",t_udpth:\"UDP-Flood Packets Threshold\",t_sync:\"Enable TCP-SYN-Flood Attack Filtering\",t_syncth:\"TCP-SYN-Flood Packets Threshold\",t_denywan:\"Forbid Ping Packet From WAN Port\",t_denylan:\"Forbid Ping Packet From LAN Port\",t_list:\"Blocked DOS Host List\"},ddos_host:{t_ip:\"Host IP Address\",t_mac:\"Host MAC Address\",t_clear:\"Clear All\"},local:{et:\"Local Management\",t_defrule:\"Management Rules\",t_all:\"All\",t_cet:\"Only\",t_rule1:\"the PCs on the LAN are allowed to access the Router's Web-Based Utility\",t_rule2:\"the PCs listed can browse the built-in web pages to perform Administrator tasks\",t_mac1:\"MAC\",t_curmac:\"Your PC's MAC Address\"},remote:{et:\"Remote Management\",t_port:\"Web Management Port\",t_host:\"Remote Management IP Address\",t_for_all:\"(Enter 255.255.255.255 for all)\"},routeTbl:{et:\"System Routing Table\",t_id:\"ID\",t_dest:\"Destination Network\",t_mask:\"Subnet Mask\",t_gw:\"Gateway\",t_intf:\"Interface\"},fw6Rules:{et:\"IPv6 Firewall Rules\",t_info:\"This device can restrict Internet activity for specified IPv6 LAN hosts. You can set and combine access control rules to effectively manage your network.\",t_en:\"Enable IPv6 Firewall\",t_defrule:\"Default Filtering Rules\",t_allow:\"Allow\",t_rule1:\"the packets not specified by any filtering rules to passthrough this device.\",t_deny:\"Deny\",t_rule2:\"the packets not specified by any filtering rules to passthrough this device.\",t_note:\"Note: The device will match the incoming packet with the enabled filtering rules one by one down the list and apply to the first matching rule. If the packet is not specified by any filtering rules within the list, then the Default Filtering Rule will take effect.\",t_host:\"IPv6 LAN Host\",t_target:\"Target\",t_sche:\"Schedule\",t_rule:\"Rule\"},fw6RulesEdit:{et:\"IPv6 Firewall Rules\",t_info:\"An IPv6 Internet access control rule can be set on this page.\",t_lan:\"IPv6 LAN Host\",t_addlan:\"Add IPv6 LAN Host\",t_wan:\"IPv6 WAN Host\",t_addwan:\"Add IPv6 WAN Host\",t_sche:\"IPv6 Schedule\",t_addsche:\"Add IPv6 Schedule\",t_action:\"Action\",t_direction:\"Direction\",t_in:\"IN\",t_out:\"OUT\"},fw6Lan:{et:\"IPv6 LAN Host\",t_addr:\"IPv6 Address Info\"},fw6LanEdit:{et:\"IPv6 LAN Host\"},fw6Wan:{et:\"IPv6 WAN Host\",t_detail:\"Details\"},fw6WanEdit:{et:\"IPv6 WAN Host\"},fw6Sche:{et:\"IPv6 Task Schedule\"},fw6ScheEdit:{et:\"IPv6 Task Schedule\",t_info:\"Schedule can be set on this page.\",t_setto:\"Apply To:\",t_start:\"Start Time\",t_end:\"End Time\",t_day:\"Each Day\",t_week:\"Each Week\",t_clear:\"Clear Schedule\"},tunnel6:{et:\"IPv6 Tunnel\",t_note:\"Note: You must reconfigure the settings on this page after rebooting the device. You must also ensure the desired WAN connection is connected before you configure the tunnel.\",t_mech:\"Mechanism\",t_conftype:\"Configuration Type\",t_manual:\"Manual\",t_remote:\"Remote IPv6 Address\",t_masklen:\"IPv4 Mask Length\",t_6rdpfx:\"6RD Prefix\",t_6rdplen:\"6RD Prefix Length\",t_braddr:\"Border Relay IPv4 Address\"},trafficCtrl:{et:\"Bandwidth Control\",t_info1:\"Bandwidth control enables you to control the bandwidth for all devices on the LAN. This page allows to set Bandwidth Control parameters. Only with Bandwidth Control enabled will these rules take effect.\",t_info2:\"Bandwidth control enables you to control the bandwidth for all devices on the LAN. This page allows to set Bandwidth Control parameters, IPTV Bandwidth Guarantee and VoIP Bandwidth Guarantee. Only with Bandwidth Control enabled will these rules take effect.\",t_info3:\"Bandwidth control enables you to control the bandwidth for all devices on the LAN. This page allows to set Bandwidth Control parameters and the VoIP Guarantee Bandwidth. Only with Bandwidth Control enabled will these rules take effect.\",t_info4:\"Bandwidth control enables you to control the bandwidth for all devices on the LAN. This page allows to set Bandwidth Control parameters, IPTV Bandwidth Guarantee and VoIP Bandwidth Guarantee. Only with Bandwidth Control enabled will these rules take effect.\",t_note:\"Note: For optimal bandwidth control, please configure the correct Line Type and bandwidth. If you are unsure about this information, please contact your ISP for further assisstance.\",t_en:\"Enable Bandwidth Control\",t_type:\"Line Type:\",t_other:\"Other\",t_tup:\"Egress Bandwidth:\",t_tdown:\"Ingress Bandwidth:\",t_info5:\"This page allows you to set Traffic Control Rules. Traffic Control Rules will only take effect when QoS is enabled along with the Scheduler Algorithm of upstream/downstream.\",t_enVoip:\"Enable VoIP Bandwidth Guarantee\",t_graiptvon:\"Enable IPTV Bandwidth Guarantee\",t_upgrabd:\"Upstream Bandwidth Guarantee:\",t_downgrabd:\"Downstream Bandwidth Guarantee:\",t_rule:\"Bandwidth Control Rules\",t_guest_rule:\"Guest Network Bandwidth Control Rules\",t_listrule:\"Description\",t_listpri:\"Priority\",t_listupbd:\"Egress Bandwidth\",t_listdownbd:\"Ingress Bandwidth\",t_warning1:\